10. Memembership operators in and not in.

Use these operators to check whether a substring or character occurs inside another string.

Code:

text=" I love python"
print("python" in text)
print("Java" in text)
print("java" not in text)

Output:

True
False
True

VERY IMPORTANT ---> These checks are case sensitive.

code:

print("python" in "Python") # returns false as p is required smaller.

